% A zero divisor is an evaluation error, for the remainder as for division:
% the evaluation stops with no rows and a nonzero exit, naming the rule.
% share/1, whose division a filter placed before it guards, never meets
% the zero, whichever strategy evaluates it.
n(0). n(4).

share(Y) :- n(X), X > 0, Y = 12 / X.
leftover(Y) :- n(X), Y = 12 mod X.

leftover(Y)?
